# flake.lock is machine-specific, so it is deliberately not committed: it pins
# the NAR hash of /etc/nixos/machine-configuration.baked, and that content only
# ever changes with an image rebuild + recreate. A committed lock therefore
# breaks the next machine's `make switch-flake` with "NAR hash mismatch" (cold
# store) or silently serves the old content (warm store).
# Each machine locks its own copy on first use; after an image change, refresh
# a stale one with `nix flake update cm` in this directory, or delete it and
# let the next switch recreate it.
flake.lock
